===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|further}}, {{m|enm|forther}}, from {{inh|en|ang|forþor}}, {{m|ang|furþor|t=further|pos=adv}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*furþer}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*per-}} (a common preposition), equivalent to {{m|en|fore}} + {{m|en||-ther}} {{gloss|a vestigial comparative ending still present in such words as {{m|en|other}}, {{m|en|either}}, {{m|en|whether}}, and, in altered form, in {{m|en|after}}}}; or as sometimes stated, as {{suf|en|forth|er|id2=comparative}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|forder}}, {{m|sco|furder|t=further}}, {{cog|stq|foarder|t=further}}, {{cog|fy|fierder|t=further}}, {{cog|nl|verder|t=further}}, {{cog|de|fürder|t=further}}.

